<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">Reconnecting instantly after every disconnect can turn a brief server hiccup into a real outage when many clients all retry at once.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Exponential backoff with jitter spreads reconnect attempts out over time instead of every client hammering the server in the same instant.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Cap the maximum delay, reset the backoff after a sustained connection, and treat different disconnect reasons differently rather than one uniform retry policy.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
